  Modifications to apply_patch_tool_instructions.md, as reproduced in the
  DESCRIPTION constant in index.mjs, in full:

    1. The `## apply_patch` heading and the blank line after it are dropped.
    2. "Use the `apply_patch` shell command to edit files" reads "tool" instead
       of "shell command", because here it is a function tool taking one string
       argument.
    3. The trailing `You can invoke apply_patch like:` sentence and the
       `shell {"command":["apply_patch", ...]}` example are dropped, for the
       same reason.
    4. Non-ASCII punctuation is flattened: U+2011 non-breaking hyphens to `-`,
       U+201C/U+201D to `"`, U+2019 to `'`. Three lines are affected.

  The text is otherwise byte-identical, and every operation the grammar defines
  is implemented. An earlier version of this file claimed the description also
  dropped `*** Delete File:` and `*** Move to:` and their grammar productions.
  That was true when it was written and stopped being true when those two
  operations were implemented; the notice was not updated with the code. It is
  recorded here because a modification notice that under-reports what was
  reproduced is the kind that matters.

  The grammar comment in parse-patch.mjs is a transcription of six productions
  from the lark definition, not a copy of the file.

